# Si64 (2x2x2 diamond supercell): NVT molecular dynamics with a Nose-Hoover thermostat
# 1000 K production-style run. OpenMX 4.0.
# Recommended: start from Si64_NVT_VS.dat# (equilibrated coordinates + velocities) instead,
# see README.md. Remove old Si64_NVT_NH.ene / .md before a fresh run.

System.CurrrentDirectory    ./
System.Name                 Si64_NVT_NH
DATA.PATH                   /opt/openmx4.0/DFT_DATA19   # EDIT: dir containing PAO/ and VPS/
level.of.stdout             1
level.of.fileout            0          # no cube files during MD

Species.Number              1
<Definition.of.Atomic.Species
  Si   Si7.0-s2p1d1   Si_PBE19          # Quick basis; compare with Si7.0-s2p2d1 before production
Definition.of.Atomic.Species>

Atoms.Number                64
Atoms.SpeciesAndCoordinates.Unit   Ang
# 2x2x2 conventional diamond cells (a = 5.43 A) + random displacements (sigma 0.05 A).
# The displacements give non-zero forces, so the velocity scaling has kinetic energy to scale.
